<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Samnite War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">343–341 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Samnite War was the first conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the Samnites of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a>. It began in 343 BCE when the Samnites attacked the Sidicini and then Capua, which appealed to Rome. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> describes Roman victories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, though his account is doubted. The war ended in 341 BCE, and Rome's foothold in Campania began its expansion into southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div>
